{"text": "11. Pinances\n\nour objective is to realize as much revenue as po:\nbefore tournament play begins. Tt will be P & P's\nresponsibility to: manage all finances; maximize revenues;\nminimize operations cost via strong negotiations and\nbarter arrangements; and submit all expenditures to\nLorillard.\n\nsible\n\na. Payment Schedule\n\nLorillard will issue checks designated for deposit\nin theyOperating Account for each tournament in\n; oon accordance with the following schedule:\n\nNew York Tournament Los Angeles Tournament\nby lO48i\u00a2t= 7 \u00a7 30,000 on 1/3/77 $30,000\non 1/3/77 30,000 on. 4/3/77\u201d 20,000\non 4/3/78: 50,000 on 7/5/77 _40,000\nTotal $110,000 \u2018Total $90,000\n\nPeriodic (weekly/monthly) statements of the balance\nof each respective account will be made to Lorillard.\nA detailed reconciliation of each account will be\nprovided to Lorillard at the close of each calendar -\nquarter. Furthermore, no expenditure in excess of\n$3,000 will be committed to by People and Properties\nwithout authorization by Lorillard. A procedure\nof anticipating and-authorizing estimated costs in\nadvance of actual payment will be utilized where possible.\n\nAfter each tournament, the Operating Accounts will\nbe closed-and the unspent balance will be returned to\nLorillara.\n\nb. Revenue Reporting\n\nPeople and Properties will provide Lorillard with a\ndetailed accounting of revenues for cach tournament.\nAll revenues tron each tournament will be deposited in an\npout Mees nccounte. Winners! purse money and the amount due. He\nbenefiting charity will be drawn fron this account.\n\nIn the event revenues exceed disbursenents from the\naccount, the balance will revert back to Lorillard.\nShould disbursements exceed revenues, the balance\nwill be provided from the tournament Operating Account.\n\nOLEPELOS",
